WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.137
Most Ansible disasters
come from three failures.

2
00:00:03.137 --> 00:00:04.924
The first is blast radius,

3
00:00:04.924 --> 00:00:09.175
where one playbook aimed too
wide changes every host at once.

4
00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:13.827
So run in check mode first, target
narrowly, and change in small batches,

5
00:00:13.827 --> 00:00:17.837
where the first batch is a canary
and a failure stops the rest.

6
00:00:17.837 --> 00:00:23.537
The second is inventory drift, where a
hand-kept host list disagrees with reality.

7
00:00:23.537 --> 00:00:27.214
Generate the inventory from
the C M D B on every run,

8
00:00:27.214 --> 00:00:30.263
and fail on a bad record
rather than guess.

9
00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:32.237
The third is credential sprawl.

10
00:00:32.237 --> 00:00:36.387
Keep credentials in one controller,
and keep secrets out of the output.

11
00:00:36.387 --> 00:00:41.063
A strict lint profile on every pull
request makes much of this automatic.

12
00:00:41.063 --> 00:00:42.120
Four more to go.
